        "original_id": "2ed7f4e4-15db-56b3-b15c-2864dd88596f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Quagmire, Seth MacFarlane, Brian Griffin, Cheryl Tiegs\n- Roles: show creator, voice actor, actress\n- Works: Family Guy, Ted, Ted 2, A Million Ways to Die in the West, Tiegs for Two\n- Concepts: 1950s party-animal clichés, rat-pack era\n\nFacts:\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted\" in 2012.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"A Million Ways to Die in the West\" in 2014.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted 2\" in 2015.\n- Seth MacFarlane, the show's creator and voice actor, described Glenn Quagmire as \"an appalling human being who is still caught in the rat-pack era\" based on anachronistic 1950s party-animal clichés.\n- In the episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Brian Griffin fails again at getting a date and seeks advice from his sex-crazed neighbor Glenn Quagmire.\n- In the episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Glenn Quagmire is also pursuing his ex-lover, actress Cheryl Tiegs.",
